From 62e3daa35e0fa8c9334d6399c82a17f7f93bd31a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KnutMann <knutmann@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 02:18:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/39] Give the receipt case back its break

The union-style conflict resolution that stacked the receipt and
reaction commits onto this branch sliced the break statement out from
between the two cases. Every receipt fell through into the reaction
handler and emitted a gowhatsapp-reaction signal with a NULL emoji,
which a front-end reads as: this sender removed their reaction. A
receipt arriving for a message someone had reacted to could silently
clear the chip. The pull request branches both carry their breaks;
only this combined branch had lost one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
