Subject: [PATCH 16/39] Ask only when the user opens a conversation, and only
 once linked

Two things the first cut got wrong. A conversation also comes into being
when a message arrives for a chat that had none, which read as the user
opening it and would have pulled a heap of old messages in underneath
the new one. Requests are now held for the length of a display, which is
the same guard that stops fetched history from asking for more history.

And the anchor was read from the device store before checking there is a
device: a conversation opened on an account that has not been linked to
a phone yet dereferenced nothing at all.

