From 12e90e3b7ff2e4511caa78664685c81bdf27b81d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KnutMann <knutmann@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 04:09:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/39] Say at linking time that this device can take history
 on demand

The request went out and the server acknowledged it, and the phone never
answered. The reason is a line this plug-in has carried since before any
of it could be parsed: it replaced the whole history configuration with
a minimum, which dropped every capability whatsmeow announces along with
it, among them the readiness to receive history on demand. Those
properties travel in the pairing payload only, never at login, so a
device that was linked without them will not be sent what it never said
it could take.

The two limits that matter for the push at linking time stay, since a
large bootstrap payload would still only be downloaded and thrown away.
Everything else is left as whatsmeow filled it in, and the on-demand
readiness is stated outright. An already linked device keeps the
properties it was linked with; only linking again announces these.

