From 9496126591d431f2fe921f8742a68b6931595328 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KnutMann <knutmann@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 19:37:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/39] A video plays where it was sent, not behind a transfer
 prompt

Videos were the one kind of media still routed through the file transfer
mechanism: an accept-first prompt whose sender is deliberately rewritten to the
group JID, because libpurple transfers know no groups. In Adium that came out
as "120363...@g.us offers to send the file ef7dc...mp4" - your own video, sent
from your own phone, presented as a stranger's incoming file named after a
hash. The transfer prompt also writes its offer line on a later runloop turn,
outside the window during which history requests are suppressed, so the
conversation it created counted as user-opened and pulled the whole history in
UNDER the offer lines.

A video now takes the inline path the other media already take: downloaded to
the temporary directory (deduplicated by content hash), kept there for
playback, and announced as a file link under the AdiumVideo_ name - the same
convention the voice notes established, which the front-end swaps for a player.
Because the line goes through the ordinary message path, the sender stays the
real sender: a video of one's own reads as one's own, a video in a group names
the person, and the conversation it may create counts as message-created, which
keeps the history fetch out from under it.

Attachment mode still hands every file to the transfer mechanism, untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
