From 289b6406b9c6a06f25f9a442bbee009542768656 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KnutMann <knutmann@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 19:52:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 26/39] A history replay shows the media it already has

A conversation replayed from the phone rendered every attachment as a
placeholder line, "[Sent a video.]", even when the video in question had just
arrived live and its file was still lying in the temporary directory. The
history handler now looks exactly there before settling for the placeholder:
videos and images stay on disk under their content-hash names (the one file
still removed is the voice note's downloaded Opus, whose decoded WAV beside it
is what playback uses), so a replayed line can point at the very file the live
message showed. Where the file is not there - never received live, or the
directory was cleaned - the placeholder stands as before.

Such a line is ready-made HTML, a link at a local file with the caption
escaped beside it, and everything else the history emits is prose for the
display path to escape. The history entry therefore says which of the two it
carries, a new text subtype carries that through the bridge, and the display
glue skips the escaping for the one and keeps it for the other.

Images gain from the same look-up: a replayed image message links its kept
file, which the front-end swaps back into a picture.

