From 49d8c04bdc9ea9e990bc13106a7ae83b1bd7d8e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KnutMann <knutmann@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 21:56:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 31/39] Two dormant slips: a directory nobody can write, an
 else that went missing

The profile-picture persist folder was created with mode 0x755. That is hex,
not octal: permission 03525, owner r-x, no write, so the file the directory
was made for could never be put into it. Upstream filed this against itself
as issue #260 and then fixed the Go side, where the mode was already octal
and correct; the C literal is the one that bites.

Next to it, the bridge-compatibility branch in send_message duplicated the
raw message and then fell straight into the strip-HTML block, because the
else between them was never written. The duplicate leaked and the bridge
behaviour was dead on arrival.

Neither is reachable under Adium defaults, the path template stays empty and
the bridge option is never set, but both are wrong in any tree that carries
them, and this tree carried both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
