From: KnutMann <knutmann@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 21:56:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 33/39] A shared contact card shows its name and numbers

A contact shared into a chat arrives as a ContactMessage, or several inside
a ContactsArrayMessage, and neither carries conversation text, so the chat
showed nothing at all: the one message type that vanished without a trace
(upstream issue #207). Now the display name and the telephone numbers from
the vCard become a line of text, in live messages and in replayed history
alike, and a reaction to such a message calls it a contact card instead of
a message of unknown type.

The vCard is read only as far as that: lines are unfolded per RFC 2425,
group prefixes like item1.TEL are accepted, and the TEL values are carried
over verbatim, never interpreted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 handle_contact.go | 83 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 handle_history.go |  3 ++
 handle_message.go |  4 +++
