Replies and reactions resolve a message id against the cache, and the
phone's history answer is by construction the set of messages not in it:
request_history asks for what lies before the newest cached line. So the
lines most tempting to reply to, the ones just restored, could not be
quoted, and the send failed late, in a goroutine, after the front-end had
already displayed the message as sent.

Every displayed history line now enters the cache under its id. Additions
during the burst skip the per-addition persist, one write at the end covers
them all; and an id already cached is left as it stands, so replaying a
line the cache already holds cannot push live messages out.

Contact cards join the field-by-field copy. Without that, the check the
contact-card commit added could never fire, a reaction to a card still said
"message of unknown type", and quoting one sent an empty quote.

