From b60b65da2f1d1611410a478ac546c9d65ff64163 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KnutMann <knutmann@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 23:37:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 39/39] The history fetch answers to bare numbers, and copies
 no locks

Extracting the feature for upstream (#263) meant reviewing it against a
plain libpurple front-end, and three of the findings hold in this tree too.
types.ParseJID reads a "+number" conversation name as a bare server name,
without error, so such a conversation silently never fetched; the plug-in's
own parseJID resolves it. The cache helpers copied whole CachedMessage
values, carrying the embedded protobuf's do-not-copy marker past go vet;
the anchor now takes scalars and the gap fill takes scalars plus a pointer,
both gathered under the lock. And the StorageQuotaMb limit upstream had
pinned to 1 MB was dropped when the struct replacement became field sets,
quietly announcing a 10 GB quota at linking time; it is pinned again.
The anchored request also logs itself now, as SETTINGS.md promises.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 handle_history.go | 91 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------------
 login.go          |  1 +
 2 files changed, 64 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)

